{
  "_about": [
    "Every MCP server `chewbacca mcp` can add. One entry per server, read by tools/mcp_setup.py.",
    "Each http url was probed live on 2026-11-02 (200, or 401 with OAuth metadata) and each",
    "package was looked up on npm or PyPI the same day. `chewbacca mcp verify` reruns both.",
    "auth: none (works at once), oauth (a browser sign-in, opened by `chewbacca mcp add`),",
    "key (a key you paste once), gh (reuses the GitHub CLI's sign-in), kit (ships with Chewbacca).",
    "Not here on purpose: Slack, Box and HubSpot's servers accept no self-registered client,",
    "so a one-command add fails at sign-in; use their claude.ai connectors. Vercel is off on",
    "Caleb's Mac (vercel-guard). Togari and Medha are Amber-internal and carry private tokens.",
    "memory and filesystem came from mcp-manager's curated catalog (Carlton Aikins, MIT), 2026-11-02."
  ],
